 /// generating hover responses. It can be rendered as a hover panel, or
 /// embedding clients can use the structured information to provide their own
 /// UI.
+/// What a hover provider adds to the hover of a declaration: an optional heading
+/// and lines of plain text, shown after the declaration's type and parameters.
+struct HoverSection {
+  std::string Heading;
+  std::vector<std::string> Lines;
+};
+
+/// A hook for plugins that run in clangd's process: a function registered here
+/// is called for every declaration that is hovered and may fill in a section
+/// (it returns whether it did). clangd knows nothing of what a provider says;
+/// the plugin decides how it learns it, for example from an attribute it
+/// attached to the declaration. The prototype uses only clang's AST and
+/// standard types, so a plugin can declare it without clangd's headers.
+using HoverProvider = bool (*)(const NamedDecl &D, HoverSection &Section);
+void registerHoverProvider(HoverProvider Provider);
+
 struct HoverInfo {
   /// Contains pretty-printed type and desugared type
